WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.240
How I think my role has had an impact
well, I think I was saying

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.460
to you before briefly like

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.080
With the recruiting campaign, we launched
a massive recruiting campaign

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.100
at the station over

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:16.960
2019 -2020 where we just literally
recruited a lot of Amapiano DJs

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.640
a lot of Afro beat DJs

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.300
Cruted a lot of media personalities around
the city

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.840
Just a lot of people who we felt would do
while in radio but weren't

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.160
necessarily being offered the opportunity
to do it

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:35.600
And then we implemented digital media into
promoting

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.140
our station and our shows, which

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.280
not a lot of radio stations do,
particularly community radio stations.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.860
So we made sure we're always recording
radio shows, we're always

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:46.780
allowing the presenters

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:52.140
to do extra content, whether it's private
week or Asian

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.940
Heritage Month or Black History Month

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.600
will do like an extra bit of digital
content to then put up on our

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.720
social media and encourage

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.640
people to come listen to the radio show
where we'll do a full show

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.240
based around

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.040
whatever the content is at that time.
